<description>
Connect the blue marker to the red marker with a green shortest king-move path.

Input structure
- A mostly background grid contains exactly one blue pixel and one red pixel.
- The marker pixels are separated in both row and column.

Rule
- Preserve the input pixels.
- Starting next to the blue pixel, paint green diagonal steps toward the red
  pixel until one diagonal step remains.
- Paint the remaining straight middle run along the longer axis, leaving the
  final diagonal step into the red pixel unpainted.

Key insight
- The path is a Chebyshev-shortest route whose straight segment absorbs the
  unequal row and column distances between the two markers.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "single blue marker pixel s",
  "dst": "single red marker pixel d",
  "path": "Chebyshev-shortest path from s toward d: diagonal steps first, then a straight run along the longer axis, with the final step diagonal into d",
  "trajectory": "paint intermediate background pixels green",
  "transform": "preserve the blue/red markers and all other input pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-16 rows x 12-16 cols, black background
  markers:
    blue: exactly 1 pixel (src)
    red: exactly 1 pixel (dst)
    no other non-background pixels
  placement:
    markers in different quadrants (differ in both row and col halves) [observed]
    row_dist: 7-12, col_dist: 3-10
    row_dist != col_dist (required)
    chebyshev_dist: 9-12 [observed]
    markers 0-3 cells from nearest edge [observed]
  path_rule: |
    Chebyshev-shortest king-move path from blue toward red, painted green:
    1. (min_axis - 1) diagonal steps from blue toward red
    2. |row_dist - col_dist| straight steps along the longer axis
    3. Final diagonal step into red is NOT painted
    Total green pixels = chebyshev_dist - 1
  path_clearance: all path cells must be background in input (trivially satisfied since input is just 2 pixels on blank grid)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input is trivially two pixels on blank grid)
  steps:
